@document.meta
title: Norg guide
description: A tour of the syntax Morg can render
authors: [
  morg
]
created: 2026-10-20
@end

Morg is a viewer for {https://github.com/nvim-neorg/neorg}[Neorg] files.
Tap a section title to fold or unfold it.

* Inline markup
  Norg has *bold*, /italic/, _underline_, -strikethrough-, !spoiler!,
  superscript like E = mc:^2^, subscript like H:,2,:O, `inline code`,
  math like $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ and variables like &name&.
  They can be nested: */bold and italic/*, *bold with _underline_ inside*.
  Free-form modifiers allow spaces: `| code with spaces |`.
  Characters are escaped with a backslash: \*this is not bold\*.
  A %hidden% comment is dimmed.

* Lists
** Unordered
   - First item
   - Second item
   -- Nested item
   --- Even deeper
   - Back to the first level with a long text that should reflow
     over several lines without losing the item indentation.

** Ordered
   ~ Make coffee
   ~ Open Neovim
   ~~ Run `:Neorg index`
   ~~ Write notes
   ~ Save

** Tasks
   - (x) Install Flutter with mise
   - (-) Write the Norg parser
   - ( ) Publish the app
   - (!) Fix the urgent bug
   - (?) Decide the final name
   - (=) Git integration on hold
   - (+) Review notes every week
   - (_) Discarded idea

* (-) Heading with a status
  Headings can carry a task status too.

* Quotes
  > Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.
  >> A quote inside another quote.

* Code blocks
  @code dart
  void main() {
    final greeting = 'Hello, Norg';
    print(greeting);
  }
  @end

  @code lua
  require("neorg").setup({
    load = { ["core.defaults"] = {} },
  })
  @end

* Tables
  @table
  | Modifier  | Character | Example  |
  |-----------|-----------|----------|
  | Bold      | `*`       | *text*   |
  | Italic    | `/`       | /text/   |
  | Code      | backtick  | `text`   |
  @end

* Definitions and footnotes
  $ Norg
  The file format of Neorg, designed for note taking.

  $$ Neorg
  A Neovim plugin.

  Organizes notes, tasks and journals.
  $$

  ^ Note 1
  Footnotes use the `^` character.

* Links
  - URL: {https://neovim.io}
  - With a description: {https://github.com/nvim-neorg/norg-specs}[Norg specification]
  - To a heading: {* Tables}[go to Tables]
  - To a file: {:notes/journal:}

* Special blocks
  |details More information
  This content lives inside a foldable `|details` block.
  |end

  |comment
  This is a comment.
  |end

  |example
  * Example heading
  - list *not* rendered
  |end

___

End of the guide.
